.\" mdsd — Markdown <-> SabyDoc converter
.TH MDSD 1 "2026" "mdsd 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdsd \- Markdown to SabyDoc format converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdsd
.I INPUT.md
.RB [ \-o
.IR OUTPUT.sabydoc ]
.RB [ \-\-title\ TEXT ]
.RB [ \-\-page\-name\ NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-strict ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Converts Markdown (CommonMark subset + GFM: tables, task lists, strikethrough,
links, HTML subset) to SabyDoc document format. The output `.sabydoc` file is
a ZIP archive without compression containing widget markup. Document title is
taken from front matter (\fBtitle:\fP), then from \fB\-\-title\fP, then from
the filename stem.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" "\fR, "\fB \-\-output " FILE
Output file path (default: same as INPUT with .sabydoc extension).
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TEXT"
Document title (documentHeader).
.TP
.BI \-\-page\-name " NAME"
Page name (default: "Basic").
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Treat warnings as errors (exit code 3).
.TP
.BR "\-r\fR, "\fB \-\-reverse
Reserved for reverse conversion (sabydoc -> md). Not yet implemented.
.SH EXIT CODES
0 — success; 1 — I/O error; 2 — invalid arguments;
3 — warnings present with \fB\-\-strict\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full description of supported constructs and limitations in README.md.
